## ⚙️ System Modules and Technologies
TFLCoMentor is divided into multiple modules. Each module handles a specific set of responsibilities.

| No. | Module                    | Technology            | Responsibilities                                                        |
| --- | ------------------------- | --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| 1   | Skill Taxonomy Module     | Java                  | Manages subjects, concepts, skill levels, and prerequisites.            |
| 2   | Evaluation Content Module | Java                  | Manages question banks, coding problems, projects, and concept mapping. |
| 3   | Assessment Module         | .NET                  | Creates tests, schedules assessments, and manages candidate attempts.   |
| 4   | Evaluation Module         | Node.js               | Processes candidate submissions and performs automated grading.         |
| 5   | Insight Module            | .NET – Future Phase   | Supports performance tracking, rankings, and analytics dashboards.      |
| 6   | Growth Module             | Python – Future Phase | Supports AI-based recommendations and concept improvement tracking.     |
| 7   | Membership & Roles Module | Node.js               | Handles user authentication, authorization, and role management.        |


### 1. Skill Taxonomy Module – Java
This module maintains the platform's skill structure and relationships between learning concepts.
**Responsibilities:**
* Manage subjects and technical skills.
* Organize concepts and topics.
* Define skill levels.
* Maintain prerequisite relationships.
* Map concepts to relevant skills.


### 2. Evaluation Content Module – Java
This module manages educational and assessment content.
**Responsibilities:**

* Maintain the question bank.
* Manage coding problems and projects.
* Organize learning and assessment content.
* Map questions to concepts and skills.
* Support content creation and review workflows.

### 3. Assessment Module – .NET
This module manages assessment creation, scheduling, and student attempts.
**Responsibilities:**
* Create and configure assessments.
* Schedule assessments.
* Assign assessments to students.
* Manage candidate attempts.
* Track assessment status.
* Store assessment-related information.

### 4. Evaluation Module – Node.js
This module evaluates student submissions and processes assessment results.
**Responsibilities:**
* Receive candidate submissions.
* Process answers and coding solutions.
* Execute automated grading workflows.
* Evaluate submissions against defined criteria.
* Generate evaluation results.
* Return results to the relevant system components.
*Note: Coding submissions should be executed in an appropriately isolated and secured environment.*

### 5. Insight Module – .NET (Future Phase)
The Insight Module will provide advanced performance analysis and reporting capabilities.
**Planned Responsibilities:**
* Track student performance.
* Analyze assessment results.
* Generate rankings and performance reports.
* Provide analytics dashboards.
* Identify strengths and improvement areas.

### 6. Growth Module – Python (Future Phase)
The Growth Module will focus on personalized learning and skill improvement.
**Planned Responsibilities:**
* Generate AI-based learning recommendations.
* Identify concepts requiring improvement.
* Track concept mastery over time.
* Recommend relevant learning resources.
* Support personalized learning paths.


### 7. Membership & Roles Module – Node.js
This module manges user identity, access, and permissions across the platform.
**Responsibilities:**
* Handle user registration and login.
* Manage authentication.
* Implement role-based authorization.
* Manage user roles and permissions.
* Support access control for different dashboards.
* Manage relevant user account operations.

